    In the name of Allah, most merciful and most compassionate
    Preface
    It is a matter of great pleasure for the Central Statistics Organization ( CSO ), to publish the
    Afghanistan Population Estimates for the year 1397 ( 2018 -19 ), In Dari, Pashto and English
    Languages . It is hoped that this publication respond to some urgent population data needs of policy
    , decision makers and researchers.
    The Population Estimates 1397(2018-19) has been done on the basis of the data obtained from the 1381-
    1384 (2003-05) Household Listing ( HHL ). The formula, Pt =Po ert has been used to calculate the
    estimated population. Where : Pt is Estimated Population , Po Base Year Population, e , Base of
    Natural Logarithm , r , Population Growth Rate and t Time Interval .
    Due to existence of more than three decades of war and conflict in the country, it has not been possible
    to conduct the second population census, after the population census 1979 so far. The settled population
    of the country, by administrative units, urban, rural and sex is estimated which covers 34 provinces (364
    original Districts, 23 Temporary districts and 34 provincial center). It may also be noted that 66 cities of
    the country are also included in the total of 421 administrative units.
    The total population of the country in 1397 (2018 -19) is estimated to be about 31.6 million persons.
    Around 16.1 million persons of this figure are men and 15.5 million persons are women. In1397(2018-
    19) out of 31.6 million population, 22.6 million persons (71.5 % ) live in rural areas 7.5 million
    persons (23.7 %) in urban areas and 1.5 million persons (4.8%) are nomad population.
    Regarding to the Nomadic Population it should be mentioned, that since1358(1979)due to lack of
    accurate data nomadic population is estimated as 1.5 million prersons.
    It has to be mentioned that in the current year population estimate base year population of Paktika,
    Daikunkdi, Helmand and Zabul provinces , which, due to late arrival of Household listing data from
    the field, was not taken into account in the past are considered in the base year and population of these
    provinces are estimated like other provinces.
    The Central Statistics Organization hopes that the Population Estimation of the country meets some of the
    urgent needs of population data users at the same time we hope that with conduct of the second population
    and housing census of the country we provide users with up to date reliable and comprehensive data.
    Central Statistics Organization
